% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement `domain_types`: Zod schemas and parse helpers for the frozen SiteVelocity domain types.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/domain-types.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Provides Zod schemas and boundary parse helpers for Fact, Unknown, Conflict, Evidence, Finding, Provenance, and Diagnostic so every module validates unknown inputs the same way.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"parseFact","signature":"(input: unknown, valueSchema: z.ZodType<T>) -> ParseOk<Fact<T>> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<Fact<T>> | ParseErr"},
  {"name":"parseEvidence","signature":"(input: unknown) -> ParseOk<Evidence> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<Evidence> | ParseErr"},
  {"name":"parseFinding","signature":"(input: unknown) -> ParseOk<Finding> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<Finding> | ParseErr"},
  {"name":"parseSourceIdentity","signature":"(input: unknown) -> ParseOk<SourceIdentity> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<SourceIdentity> | ParseErr"},
  {"name":"parseConflict","signature":"(input: unknown, valueSchema: z.ZodType<T>) -> ParseOk<Conflict<T>> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<Conflict<T>> | ParseErr"},
  {"name":"parseProvenance","signature":"(input: unknown) -> ParseOk<Provenance> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<Provenance> | ParseErr"},
  {"name":"parseDiagnostic","signature":"(input: unknown) -> ParseOk<Diagnostic> | ParseErr","returns":"ParseOk<Diagnostic> | ParseErr"}
]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Provide Zod schemas and parse helpers for the frozen domain types; validate unknown boundary values; return typed values or structured SchemaIssue lists.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT fetch or store evidence.
- DOES NOT research sites.
- DOES NOT score candidates or sites.
- DOES NOT compute finance outputs.
- DOES NOT call providers or import provider SDKs.
- DOES NOT map government source fields onto canonical candidates.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
known: a Fact whose status is exactly `known` and whose value is present under the value schema.
unknown: a Fact or standalone marker whose status is exactly `unknown` with a non-blank reasonCode; never implied by omission, null, zero, or false alone.
conflict: a Conflict whose status is `conflicting` and whose values array retains at least two source-backed entries.
valid: an input that satisfies the corresponding Zod schema and returns `{ ok: true, value }`.
invalid: an input that fails the corresponding Zod schema and returns `{ ok: false, issues }`.
complete: a SourceIdentity or Evidence record that includes every required field with a well-formed value.
safe: a diagnostic or schema-issue message that contains no credentials, secrets, API keys, bearer tokens, or password material.
malformed: an ID, timestamp, enum, or number that fails its declared format or domain.
finite: a number that is not NaN and not ±Infinity.
uuid: a canonical UUID string accepted by Zod's UUID checker.
schema issue: a structured `{ path, code, message }` describing one validation failure without inventing domain facts.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Model Fact as an explicit known|unknown discriminated union; omission, null, zero, and false MUST NOT implicitly mean unknown.
R2 (MUST): A conflict retains at least two incompatible values, each with a SourceIdentity; reject a one-source conflict as invalid.
R3 (MUST): Evidence retains id, source (URL and agency via SourceIdentity including retrievedAt), checksum, and payloadOrRef; reject incomplete evidence missing checksum or source.
R4 (MUST): Finding status, evidenceLevel, impact, confidence (finite 0..1), and evidenceIds follow System Design §7.4 enums and bounds.
R5 (MUST): Provenance and diagnostics use stable reason codes and non-empty safe messages; reject a diagnostic whose message is credential-like (contains substrings such as `api_key=`, `Bearer `, or `password=`).
R6 (MUST): Reject malformed uuid values, malformed timestamps, non-finite numbers, invalid enums, and confidence outside 0..1 inclusive.
R7 (MUST NOT): Import provider SDKs, expose credentials, or use provider names as domain identity.
</contract_rules>

<interface_types>

Types are declared in the included `domain-types.prompt` freeze. Export exactly:

```ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const SourceIdentitySchema: z.ZodType<SourceIdentity>;
export const FactSchema: <T>(valueSchema: z.ZodType<T>) => z.ZodType<Fact<T>>;
export const UnknownSchema: z.ZodType<Unknown>;
export const ConflictSchema: <T>(valueSchema: z.ZodType<T>) => z.ZodType<Conflict<T>>;
export const EvidenceSchema: z.ZodType<Evidence>;
export const FindingSchema: z.ZodType<Finding>;
export const ProvenanceSchema: z.ZodType<Provenance>;
export const DiagnosticSchema: z.ZodType<Diagnostic>;

export type ParseOk<T> = { ok: true; value: T };
export type ParseErr = { ok: false; issues: SchemaIssue[] };
export function parseSourceIdentity(input: unknown): ParseOk<SourceIdentity> | ParseErr;
export function parseFact<T>(input: unknown, valueSchema: z.ZodType<T>): ParseOk<Fact<T>> | ParseErr;
export function parseConflict<T>(input: unknown, valueSchema: z.ZodType<T>): ParseOk<Conflict<T>> | ParseErr;
export function parseEvidence(input: unknown): ParseOk<Evidence> | ParseErr;
export function parseFinding(input: unknown): ParseOk<Finding> | ParseErr;
export function parseProvenance(input: unknown): ParseOk<Provenance> | ParseErr;
export function parseDiagnostic(input: unknown): ParseOk<Diagnostic> | ParseErr;
```

Parse helpers MUST NOT throw for ordinary invalid input; they return `ParseErr` with safe SchemaIssue lists. Use only `zod` and local types — never `@renderinc/sdk`, `@supabase/supabase-js` as domain identity, MiniMax SDK packages, or Rtrvr SDK packages.

</interface_types>

